  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 142 AM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nPersistent upper level ridging will remain anchored across the \nsoutheast CONUS Friday. The center of the upper high will gradually \ntranslate back westward into the desert southwest by early next \nweek. ENS/GEFS mean PWAT values are very high during this timeframe, \nas monsoonal/subtropical moisture aloft flows northeastward from \nwestern Mexico on the northwest periphery of the upper level high. \nENS continues to suggest PWAT values greater than 1.7\" (which would \nbe exceeding the the 90th percentile) will be in place both Friday \nand Saturday. Several waves/pertubations will be embedded within the \nsouthwest flow aloft, and rounds of showers and thunderstorms will \nbe likely Friday and Saturday. Upslope flow behind the front along \nwith at least some instability will set the stage for locally heavy \nrainfall. Mid and upper flow supports some training/backbuilding \npotential, which could localize heavy rainfall. The 11/12Z ENS mean \nQPF through Monday has an average of 1.5 to 2.5 inches area wide. \nLocally heavier amounts will be possible where any training or \nbackbuilding of occurs. \n\nTemperatures will be below normal during the Friday through Monday \ntimeframe. This is due to a considerable amount of cloud cover and \neasterly low-level upslope flow. High temperatures ranging from the \nmid 70s to lower 80s are expected through this period. Some \nmoderation is expected Tuesday with most areas in the 80s.",
